 ## 11. Keep This File and the Log Portable
 
 `.agents/LOG.md` and `.agents/AGENT-RULES.md` are committed to the repository. They must remain plaintext Markdown, with no Replit-specific tooling required to read them. Any agent, on any platform, must be able to read and append to them with a standard text editor or file write tool.
+
+---
+
+## 12. Evidence and Provenance — Do Not Rely on "I Ran It"
+
+> Do not rely on "I ran it" as evidence. Persist the command, environment, exit
+> code, counts, duration, artifact path, checksum, and remote-state effect. If
+> stdout or exit status is lost, classify the result as UNRECORDED and rerun it.
+> Before rerunning, search the handoff logs and artifact index so an already
+> captured successful result is not repeated unnecessarily.
+
+For every setup, build, test, gate, reconstruction, or handoff action, append one
+machine-readable record (JSONL preferred, append-only or versioned) containing:
+UTC timestamp; agent/session/workspace identifier; repository, branch, and exact
+commit (plus parent, tree, and patch checksum when applicable); runtime versions
+(Node, pnpm, PostgreSQL, OS/container); the exact command or tool action; the
+test/gate name; duration; exit code; test counts and failed-test details; the
+artifact/log path and its checksum; whether the action changed files, refs, or
+remote state; whether the result is reproducible; and the next action plus
+whether approval is required. Keep a concise human-readable summary alongside.
+
+Classify every result as exactly one of:
+
+- **PASS** — captured and reproducible
+- **FAIL** — captured with diagnosis
+- **BLOCKED** — external prerequisite missing
+- **UNRECORDED** — output lost or tool timeout; must rerun
+- **NOT_RUN** — deliberately not executed
+
+Never record tokens, passwords, database URLs, private keys, secrets, or
+unnecessary personal data; redact command output before persistence (this
+extends Rule 9 to captured evidence).
